     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "'Top-k sampling in LLMs refers to a method where, during the generation of text, the model selects from the top k most likely next tokens based on their predicted probabilities. This approach allows for more diverse and relevant outputs compared to purely deterministic methods, as it samples from a restricted set of options rather than always choosing the highest probability token.'"
      ]
     },
